{"name":"Rare White Raven","hex":"#e8dbdf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rare","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very uncommon; scarce.","Small in number (but not unusual); infrequent; sparse."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A scarce or uncommon item."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rare"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"},{"term":"raven","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several, generally large, species of birds in the genus Corvus with lustrous black plumage; especially the common raven (Corvus corax).","A jet-black, often glossy, colour, like that of the plumage of a raven (etymology 1, noun sense 1)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the jet-black and often glossy colour of the plumage of a raven (etymology 1, noun sense 1)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raven"}],"entries":[{"title":"Raven","blocks":[{"text":"A raven is any of several large-bodied passerine bird species in the genus Corvus. These species do not form a single taxonomic group within the genus. There is no consistent distinction between crows and ravens; the two names are assigned to different species mainly by size."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/3782_Common_Raven_in_flight.jpg/330px-3782_Common_Raven_in_flight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raven","wikidata":"Q8335"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"